1. Product Data Creation

Created 50 product documents in the products collection using a JavaScript for loop.

for (let i = 1; i <= 50; i++) {
    db.products.insertOne({
        productId: i,
        productName: "Product " + i,
        category:
            i % 5 === 0 ? "Laptop" :
            i % 5 === 1 ? "Mobile" :
            i % 5 === 2 ? "Headphones" :
            i % 5 === 3 ? "Keyboard" :
                          "Mouse",
        brand:
            i % 3 === 0 ? "Dell" :
            i % 3 === 1 ? "Samsung" :
                          "HP",
        price: 1000 + (i * 500),
        stock: 10 + i,
        rating: 3 + ((i % 3) * 0.5),
        inStock: i % 4 !== 0,
        tags: [
            "electronics",
            i % 2 === 0 ? "featured" : "new"
        ],
        seller: {
            sellerId: 1000 + i,
            sellerName: "Seller " + i
        },
        createdAt: new Date()
    });
}
2. Updating Product 20 Price

Updated the price of Product 20 using updateMany().

db.products.updateMany(
    { productId: 20 },
    { $set: { price: 17000 } }
)

Result:

acknowledged: true
matchedCount: 2
modifiedCount: 2

Both documents with productId: 20 were updated.

3. Updating Product 20 Seller Name

Updated the seller name of the first matching Product 20 document.

db.products.updateOne(
    { productId: 20 },
    { $set: { "seller.sellerName": "Aditya Store" } }
)

Result:

acknowledged: true
matchedCount: 1
modifiedCount: 1

The updated document contains:

seller: {
    sellerId: 1020,
    sellerName: "Aditya Store"
}

The second Product 20 document remained:

seller: {
    sellerId: 1020,
    sellerName: "Seller 20"
}
4. Increasing Product 20 Stock

Increased the stock of the first matching Product 20 document by 20.

db.products.updateOne(
    { productId: 20 },
    { $inc: { stock: 20 } }
)

The stock changed from:

30

to:

50
