6. Removing the Rating Field

Removed the rating field from the first matching Product 20 document.

db.products.updateOne(
    { productId: 20 },
    { $unset: { rating: "" } }
)

Result:

acknowledged: true
matchedCount: 1
modifiedCount: 1
7. MongoDB Operators Practiced
$set

Used to create or modify a field.

db.products.updateOne(
    { productId: 20 },
    { $set: { price: 17000 } }
)
$inc

Used to increase or decrease a numeric field.

db.products.updateOne(
    { productId: 20 },
    { $inc: { stock: 20 } }
)
$unset

Used to remove a field.

db.products.updateOne(
    { productId: 20 },
    { $unset: { rating: "" } }
)
Nested Field Update

Used dot notation to update a nested field.

"seller.sellerName"

Example:

db.products.updateOne(
    { productId: 20 },
    { $set: { "seller.sellerName": "Aditya Store" } }
)
